-Oh, yeah.

1502
01:21:21,860 --> 01:21:23,659
It is incredibly territorial.

1503
01:21:23,660 --> 01:21:25,760
They kill more people
than lions out there.

1504
01:21:25,930 --> 01:21:27,460
Yep.

1505
01:21:27,630 --> 01:21:29,630
<i>One of Africa's
deadliest animals,</i>

1506
01:21:29,800 --> 01:21:33,659
<i>hippos have the jaw strength
three times that of a lion.</i>

1507
01:21:33,660 --> 01:21:36,730
<i>Their poor eyesight make
them skittish by nature,</i>

1508
01:21:36,900 --> 01:21:39,860
<i>leading to highly aggressive
and territorial behavior.</i>

1509
01:21:41,760 --> 01:21:44,030
-Jesus!
-Oh, wow!

1510
01:21:44,200 --> 01:21:46,260
I think it's a big
male and a female.

1511
01:21:46,430 --> 01:21:47,530
So I'm gonna be catfishing

1512
01:21:47,700 --> 01:21:49,060
at the other end of the river.

1513
01:21:49,230 --> 01:21:51,130
It doesn't matter where you go.

1514
01:21:51,300 --> 01:21:52,660
No, they move.

1515
01:21:52,830 --> 01:21:54,530
And they come out at night.

1516
01:21:54,700 --> 01:21:56,130
-Yep.
-No.

1517
01:21:56,300 --> 01:21:58,360
And if you're in between
them and the water hole,

1518
01:21:58,530 --> 01:22:00,659
they'll trample you
and gore you to death.

1519
01:22:00,660 --> 01:22:02,030
I think we have to keep going

1520
01:22:02,200 --> 01:22:03,960
and find the next water hole.

1521
01:22:04,130 --> 01:22:06,560
-One without hippos?
-Yeah.

1522
01:22:06,730 --> 01:22:08,559
I completely agree,
it's unsafe we stay.

1523
01:22:08,560 --> 01:22:11,260
Though the hippos
kill people all the time.

1524
01:22:11,430 --> 01:22:12,960
On first sight, we were like,

1525
01:22:13,130 --> 01:22:15,560
"Oh, my God! This is
a massive water hole."

1526
01:22:15,730 --> 01:22:19,530
And I'm thinking, "Finally,
I'm gonna catch bloody fish."

1527
01:22:19,700 --> 01:22:22,260
To see the hippos
pop up, my heart sinks,

1528
01:22:22,430 --> 01:22:24,459
none of us wanna keep going,

1529
01:22:24,460 --> 01:22:29,060
but to make a home
here would be suicide.

1530
01:22:29,230 --> 01:22:31,830
It looks like there's a
game trail that keeps going.

1531
01:22:32,000 --> 01:22:36,159
-Yeah.
-And I'm guessing, you know, all game trails...

1532
01:22:36,160 --> 01:22:37,860
-Lead to water.
-Lead to water.

1533
01:22:38,830 --> 01:22:42,030
I wanted this journey
to be over so bad,

1534
01:22:42,200 --> 01:22:45,130
but when I seen them
hippos, I knew there's no way

1535
01:22:45,300 --> 01:22:49,360
we can stay here, and
that was just soul crushing.

1536
01:22:49,530 --> 01:22:51,430
All right, guys,
let's get out of here.

1537
01:22:51,600 --> 01:22:54,759
We're making them upset.
This is not a safe place.

1538
01:22:54,760 --> 01:22:56,100
This is not where we're staying.

1539
01:22:56,260 --> 01:22:57,360
-No.
-We'll die.

1540
01:22:57,530 --> 01:22:58,859
-On to the next one.
-Let's go.

1541
01:22:58,860 --> 01:23:00,160
It's getting late.

1542
01:23:00,960 --> 01:23:02,360
He is watching us leave.

1543
01:23:04,100 --> 01:23:05,330
This sucks.

1544
01:23:21,430 --> 01:23:23,760
Oh, man. I'm getting hot.

1545
01:23:25,430 --> 01:23:27,000
-Hey, buddy.
-Hey.

1546
01:23:28,230 --> 01:23:30,730
-How you doing?
-Good, you?

1547
01:23:30,900 --> 01:23:32,460
Doing good.

1548
01:23:32,630 --> 01:23:33,730
See any animals down there?

1549
01:23:34,730 --> 01:23:36,430
-Not a damn thing.
-Nothing.

1550
01:23:41,000 --> 01:23:42,360
Well, Teal and I
had a conversation

1551
01:23:42,430 --> 01:23:45,359
while you were down the water,
and we've made the decision

1552
01:23:45,360 --> 01:23:46,560
we have to leave.

1553
01:23:49,030 --> 01:23:50,830
We gotta go.

1554
01:23:51,000 --> 01:23:52,160
We need to get back on track.

1555
01:23:52,300 --> 01:23:55,100
It's not about staying
and doing anything.

1556
01:23:55,260 --> 01:23:57,830
It's about moving
on, it's a long way

1557
01:23:58,000 --> 01:24:00,460
-to the next waterhole.
-Yeah.

1558
01:24:00,630 --> 01:24:01,630
Apart from the turtles,

1559
01:24:01,631 --> 01:24:03,276
I haven't seen an animal
since we've been here.

1560
01:24:03,300 --> 01:24:04,906
So we're wanting to push
through and see if there's

1561
01:24:04,930 --> 01:24:07,530
a place with a lot
more opportunities.

1562
01:24:07,700 --> 01:24:09,430
We would love to
have you come with us.

1563
01:24:13,260 --> 01:24:14,730
No?

1564
01:24:14,900 --> 01:24:16,560
There's nothing here.

1565
01:24:17,660 --> 01:24:20,659
If we go forward to
this oasis or something,

1566
01:24:20,660 --> 01:24:22,130
and it's got more water,

1567
01:24:22,300 --> 01:24:24,159
to me, that's...
its... harder target.

1568
01:24:24,160 --> 01:24:26,559
-Mm-hmm.
-I wanna continue to fight

1569
01:24:26,560 --> 01:24:28,759
and get really beat this place.

1570
01:24:28,760 --> 01:24:31,530
That goal still seems
attainable to me.

1571
01:24:31,700 --> 01:24:32,799
They may not see it.

1572
01:24:32,800 --> 01:24:36,359
They don't know how big
of a commitment to my heart

1573
01:24:36,360 --> 01:24:39,759
it has been to
succeed at this task.

1574
01:24:39,760 --> 01:24:41,680
So when they wanna get
out of here, I understand.

1575
01:24:41,730 --> 01:24:43,760
It is not a desirable place.

1576
01:24:43,930 --> 01:24:46,000
But my heart belongs
here with my task,

1577
01:24:46,160 --> 01:24:48,259
with what I wanna
do, with who I am,

1578
01:24:48,260 --> 01:24:49,960
and how I accomplish my goals.

1579
01:24:52,430 --> 01:24:54,460
This isn't to try and force
your hand or anything.

1580
01:24:56,160 --> 01:24:58,430
If you think this water hole

1581
01:24:58,600 --> 01:24:59,880
owes you an extra
couple of days,

1582
01:25:00,100 --> 01:25:02,430
we're gonna be
leaving without you.

1583
01:25:02,600 --> 01:25:05,160
We just have to have... we have
to have a hard, hard line on it.

1584
01:25:08,860 --> 01:25:10,060
Think about it.

1585
01:25:12,160 --> 01:25:13,930
I don't know yet, but we'll see.

1586
01:25:14,100 --> 01:25:15,500
We'll see what happens.

1587
01:25:17,960 --> 01:25:20,130
This land, it can consume you,

1588
01:25:20,300 --> 01:25:23,859
and it's already started on Joe,
but if this wasteland takes him,

1589
01:25:23,860 --> 01:25:25,660
it's not taking me too.

1590
01:25:25,830 --> 01:25:26,860
-Yeah.
-You never know.

